  squirrelstack whoami                            Show the active user + account
  squirrelstack users                             List logged-in users
  squirrelstack users use <email> [-g]            Pin user for cwd (or globally with -g)
  squirrelstack users use --clear [-g]            Remove the pinned user
  squirrelstack accounts                          List accounts you can access
  squirrelstack accounts use <slug> [-g]          Pin account for cwd (or globally with -g)
  squirrelstack accounts use --clear [-g]         Remove the pinned account
  squirrelstack accounts current                  Show resolved account + source
  squirrelstack errors [options]                  List open errors
  squirrelstack errors show <ID>                  Show error details with notes
  squirrelstack errors update <ID> [options]      Update error status/priority/assignee
  squirrelstack errors comment <ID> <message>     Add a note to an error
  squirrelstack errors members                    List team members (for --assign)
  squirrelstack tickets [options]                 List open helpdesk tickets
  squirrelstack tickets show <ID>                 Show ticket details with messages
  squirrelstack epics [options]                   List epics
  squirrelstack epics show <ID>                   Show an epic with its stories
  squirrelstack epics create <title> [options]    Create an epic
  squirrelstack epics update <ID> [options]       Update an epic
  squirrelstack stories [options]                 List stories
  squirrelstack stories show <ID>                 Show a story with tasks and notes
  squirrelstack stories create <title> [options]  Create a story in an epic
  squirrelstack stories update <ID> [options]     Update or move a story

User selection (in order):
  --user <email>           Flag (highest priority)
  SQUIRRELSTACK_USER       Env var
  ./.squirrelstack         Walked up from cwd (user=<email>)
  ~/.squirrelstack         Global default
  (single user)            Used when exactly one user is logged in

Account selection (in order):
  --account <slug>         Flag (highest priority)
  SQUIRRELSTACK_ACCOUNT    Env var
  ./.squirrelstack         Walked up from cwd (account=<slug>)
  ~/.squirrelstack         Global default
  (server default)         Used when your user has exactly one account

Options for 'errors':
  --status <status>     Filter: unresolved (default), resolved, ignored, all
  --severity <level>    Filter: critical, error, warning, info
  --env <environment>   Filter by environment (e.g. production)
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'errors update':
  --status <status>     Set: unresolved, resolved, ignored, always_ignored
  --priority <level>    Set: critical, high, medium, low, none
  --assign <user_id>    Assign to user (use 'none' to unassign)

Options for 'errors show':
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'tickets':
  --state <state>       Filter: open (default), new, assigned, closed, all
  --priority <level>    Filter: urgent, high, normal, low
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'tickets show':
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'epics':
  --bucket <bucket>     Filter: ongoing, now, next, future, done
  --owner <user_id>     Filter by owner
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'epics create' and 'epics update':
  --title <text>        Epic title (update only; create takes it as the first argument)
  --description <text>  Longer description
  --bucket <bucket>     ongoing, now, next, future, done (new epics can't start in now)
  --theme <label>       Theme label
  --owner <user_id>     Owner (use 'none' to unassign)
  --start <date>        Planned start, YYYY-MM-DD
  --end <date>          Planned end, YYYY-MM-DD
  --position <n>        Sort position within the bucket

Options for 'stories':
  --status <status>     Filter: backlog, ready, doing, review, done
  --epic <epic_id>      Filter by epic
  --owner <user_id>     Filter by owner
  --json                Output raw JSON

Options for 'stories create' and 'stories update':
  --epic <epic_id>      Epic the story belongs to (required on create)
  --title <text>        Story title (update only; create takes it as the first argument)
  --description <text>  Longer description
  --status <status>     backlog, ready, doing, review, done
  --points <n>          Story points: 0.5, 1, 2, 4, 8
  --owner <user_id>     Owner (use 'none' to unassign)
  --position <n>        Sort position within the status column

Options for 'epics show' and 'stories show':
  --json                Output raw JSON

Environment variables:
  SQUIRRELSTACK_TOKEN     PAT token (overrides Keychain and user selection)
  SQUIRRELSTACK_USER      Email of the logged-in user to use
  SQUIRRELSTACK_ACCOUNT   Account slug to send as X-Account-Slug
  SQUIRRELSTACK_URL       API base URL (default: https://squirrelstack.app)

Tokens are stored securely in macOS Keychain, one per user. You can log in
as multiple users and switch between them per directory or globally. On first
use, you'll be prompted to log in or paste a PAT.
